    "verdict": "Contiguous-block hold-out produces 2.5-7.7x larger prediction error than random hold-out of the same size, and the ratio grows with block size. Random hold-out therefore fails to remove information -- neighbouring wavelengths interpolate across every gap -- which is exactly the mechanism `DATA_GUIDE.md` warns about. Every robustness check in this report consequently holds out contiguous wavelength bands or whole temperature slices, never random points."
